# Changelog & Versioning

`docs/changelog.md` is the standardized transaction history of the repository.
Update it as part of completing any user-facing or notable change.

## Format

Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) and
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/) (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`).

- New work accumulates under an `## [Unreleased]` heading.
- Group entries under: `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Removed`, `Security`.
- On release, rename `[Unreleased]` to `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` and start a
  fresh `[Unreleased]` block. Bump the `version` field in `package.json` to
  match.

## When to bump

- `PATCH`: bug fixes, no API/behavior change.
- `MINOR`: backwards-compatible features.
- `MAJOR`: breaking changes.

## Entry style

Prefix every entry with its date (`YYYY-MM-DD — `) so each change is dated, not
just each release.

```
## [Unreleased]
### Added
- 2026-07-07 — Grade breakdown export to CSV.
### Fixed
- 2026-07-07 — Incorrect rounding in the carbon score calculation.
```

Keep entries concise and written for humans (the "why", not a diff dump).
Every commit that changes behavior should leave a trace here.
